  "reason": "The candidate is rejected because it asserts the existence of 'attention weights' (scalar coefficients per head/pair) as learnable parameters requiring gradient computation. This contradicts standard decoder-only transformer mechanics where attention is implemented via matrix multiplication of query and key vectors ($W_Q, W_K$), not scalar weights. The counterexample in text_1 explicitly states that gradients flow through these projection matrices, not separate 'attention weights'. Therefore, the intended fact must be corrected to reflect that backpropagation computes gradients for the projection matrices (Q, K, V) and feed-forward parameters, not non-existent scalar attention weights.",
